  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-github",
      "text": "[中文文档](README.zh.md) | English\n\nDSH Web UI 的 GitHub 与本地 Git 工作流插件。"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- GitHub Personal Access Token account management with secret-free summaries.\n- GitHub REST repository listing for github.com and GitHub Enterprise API URLs.\n- Local Git operations: clone, fast-forward pull, status, commit, push, and force-with-lease.\n- Sidebar panel with account, repository, local Git, and settings tabs.\n- Push and force push are disabled by default and are guarded on the Host side.\n- Token storage uses ~/.dsh/dsh-github.json with an atomic write and mode 0600.\n- Git HTTP authentication uses an ephemeral http.extraheader environment configuration; tokens are not placed in clone URLs or process arguments."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install in a profile",
      "text": "Download the newest `dsh-github-*.tgz` from [Releases](https://github.com/andyfan1094/dsh-github/releases) and add it to the profile:\n\n```powershell\ndsh plugin --profile web add D:\\downloads\\dsh-github-0.1.2.tgz\n```\n\nFor local development, build and install from a checkout instead:\n\npnpm install\n    pnpm run build\n    dsh plugin --profile web add link:D:\\项目\\dsh-github"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install in a profile",
      "text": "Restart the existing DSH Web process after installation. Open the GitHub sidebar entry and add a replacement token there. The plugin deliberately does not ship a token in source, package metadata, logs, or documentation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Agent tools",
      "text": "- github_auth_list, github_auth_test\n- github_repo_list\n- github_clone, github_pull, github_status\n- github_commit, github_push"
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "- DSH Host `0.1.0-rc.8` or newer compatible release.\n- Node.js `22.19.0` or newer.\n- Git must be available through the configured executable."
    },
    {
      "section": "Security",
      "text": "The account file is local configuration, not a system secret vault. Use a fine-grained GitHub token with only the repositories and permissions needed by DSH. Revoke any token pasted into chat or source control and create a new one through the panel."
    }
  ],
